<title>USA: Conn Gov. wants more bids on renaming civic center.</title>
<headline>Conn Gov. wants more bids on renaming civic center.</headline>
<dateline>HARTFORD 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Connecticut Gov. John Rowland decided to hold off on an offer to rename the Hartford Civic Center from the Phoenix Home Life Mutual Insurance Co.</p>
<p>The insurance company had offered to pay $400,000 a year for the next five years for the naming rights to the publicly owned center.</p>
<p>Rowland said there was no competitive bidding, and Connecticut Development Authority is working to solicit bids from other interested companies.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
